[Hephi test] [Bug] QoS count command ignores the times argument after cd

@paxxie2

这是从 apache/dubbo#16530 复制的代码 Issue，用于验证 Super Agent → HEPHI 插件交付链路。
原始 Issue：https://github.com/apache/dubbo/issues/16530

---

### Apache Dubbo Component

Java SDK (apache/dubbo)

### Dubbo Version

`3.3` branch (cb05763298), OpenJDK 21, macOS. The argument parsing goes back to `CountTelnetHandler` in 2.0.7 and was carried over to the QoS `CountTelnet` in #8175.

### Steps to reproduce this issue

1. Start a provider with QoS enabled and a dubbo service (here `repro.Echo` with a method `length`).
2. Connect to the QoS port and run `cd repro.Echo`, then `count length 3`.

The statistics table is printed once. Without `cd`, `count repro.Echo length 3` prints it three times, one second apart.

`CountTelnet#execute` reads the times like this:

```java
if (service == null || service.length() == 0) {
    service = args[0];
    method = args.length > 1 ? args[1] : null;
} else {
    method = args.length > 0 ? args[0] : null;
}
if (StringUtils.isNumber(method)) {
    times = method;
    method = null;
} else {
    times = args.length > 2 ? args[2] : "1";
}
```

After `cd`, the arguments are `[method, times]`, so `args[2]` does not exist and `times` falls back to `"1"`. (`count length 3 5` after `cd` runs five times.)

### What you expected to happen

`count length 3` after `cd repro.Echo` prints the table three times, like `count repro.Echo length 3`. The usage message of the command also describes `cd XxxService` as an alternative to giving the service name (`count XxxService xxxMethod 10 ... or "cd XxxService" firstly`).

### Anything else

`count 3` after `cd` (no method) already works, because a numeric first argument is taken as the times.

